{
	title: 'Concise repository agent guidance',
	spec: 'AGENTS.md holds concise, sectioned guidance for Git, rebuildable tasks, spec writing, privacy, tests, minimal code, multiple agents sharing a checkout, orchestration, progress reports and inspectable UI. Preserve the rules in the AGENTS.md artifact, including commit trailers, task traceability, private-file exclusions and safety boundaries. Apply Strunk & White without weakening requirements. Git defaults to rebase and autostash. When multiple agents share a checkout, disable autostash, never stash others’ changes, and rebase only when that checkout is clean and no other agent is editing it. Explain that agents in the same checkout share files and the Git index even without using git worktree. Avoid overlapping work. Use worktrees only read-only, to test work that others’ uncommitted edits break or to run or inspect another revision; never commit in one; claim a fix only once its commit sits in the checkout the Hal host runs from. Wrap prose at 72 columns, preserving Markdown headings, list indentation, code blocks and inline code spans. Keep wording edits separate from paragraph reflow for review. Work directly by default. Delegate only when substantial independent parallel work, independent scrutiny of risk or disputed conclusions, or isolation of a noisy investigation outweighs token, delay and coordination costs. Exclude routine searches, small edits and tightly coupled work; task count alone is insufficient. State the benefit before spawning, use the fewest agents needed and avoid duplicating their work. Give delegates bounded tasks, relevant context, deliverables and file ownership. Fresh implementers, task sizing and slot budgeting apply only to delegated work; the parent reviews and integrates results and implementers re-run ./test before pushing.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The old Git paragraph requested autostash while the shared-tree rule forbade stashing uncommitted work. Keep the requested defaults but require --no-autostash for shared worktrees, commit before rebasing, and wait for others’ uncommitted work. Removed repeated task-tracking instructions and illustrative report output, not their requirements.',
		'Correction to the preceding note: stash is intended for uncommitted work; the blanket ban was overbroad. The guidance distinguishes exclusive worktrees from shared ones: disable autostash in shared worktrees, never stash others’ changes, and rebase only with a clean, idle shared tree.',
		"An agent added a correcting task without foldInto after reading only tsk help, and git commit <paths> swept another agent's uncommitted AGENTS.md edits into its commit. AGENTS.md now requires tsk --detailed-help, a search of tasks/ before tsk add with needs/foldInto set, and hunk staging with a pathless git commit when others edited the same file.",
		'The blanket instruction to give each implementer a subagent conflicted with exceptional delegation. The orchestration section now defines the exceptions and scopes delegation mechanics to delegated work.'
	],
	needs: []
